   "insight": {
    "headline": "The mainland and Hong Kong split",
    "body": "A genuine divergence today. Shenzhen rose 1.93% and Shanghai 0.66%, while Hong Kong's Hang Seng fell 1.60%. The split is technology: Tencent -7.23%, Meituan -5.96%, Xiaomi -5.29%, all Hong Kong-listed, dragging the tech average to -5.55%. Mainland boards carry more state-linked industrial and financial names and held up better. CATL rose 1.30%. When two markets in the same country move opposite ways, the explanation is usually what is listed where, not a change in the economy."
   }
