   "insight": {
    "headline": "Japan keeps running, Europe does not",
    "body": "The Nikkei added another 2.93% after last week's 4.74%, extending the strongest run of any major market. Europe went the other way, with the FTSE down 1.39% and the CAC down 1.02%, though the DAX rose 0.46% — again, not moving as a bloc. Gold gained 0.99% while WTI crude fell 1.24%, the same divergence as last week: metals bid on rate expectations rather than war fear. For an Indian reader the relevant number remains the rupee at 95.59, still drifting weaker."
   }
